{
  "title": "Second declension: neuter and feminine nouns",
  "note": "Neuter nouns in -ον decline like λόγος, but the nominative and accusative are always the same, and the plural ends in -α: ἔργον, ἔργου, ἔργῳ, ἔργον; ἔργα, ἔργων, ἔργοις, ἔργα. A neuter plural subject usually takes a singular verb. A few -ος nouns are feminine and take ἡ: ἡ ὁδός, the road.",
